# Git commits: one feature per commit

The history is used to show how each feature started and how it grew. A commit
that bundles several features cannot be checked out to show any one of them, so
**every commit holds exactly one feature, fix, or scene change.**

## When to propose a commit

At the end of each feature that works in Play mode, before starting the next
one, propose a commit. Do not wait for a milestone. Do not commit without the
user's yes, and never push unless asked.

If uncommitted changes already span several features, split them into one
commit per feature. Never fold them into one "milestone" commit.

## The proposal

Show this and wait:

1. The commit message
2. The exact files to stage, grouped by commit if there is more than one
3. Any files left out, and why

## Message format

`type(scope): what the player or developer can now do`

- **type:** `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `scene`, `art`, `chore`
- **scope:** the system, lowercase. Reuse an existing scope before inventing one:
  `scent`, `senses`, `tutorial`, `camera`, `movement`, `upgrades`, `orbs`,
  `checkpoint`, `transitions`, `world`, `ui`, or a scene name for `scene`
  commits (`scene(level1): ...`)
- Imperative, under 72 characters, no trailing period

```
feat(scent): add wave distortion to scent trail shader
fix(camera): stop lead offset snapping on respawn
scene(level2): place upgrade orbs along the cave path
```

## Staging

- Stage by explicit path: `git add <file> <file>`. Never `git add .` or `git add -A`.
- A script, its `.meta`, and the prefab/material/shader it introduced go in the
  same commit.
- **Scene files (`.unity`)** cannot be split by hunk safely. Commit a scene with
  the feature that required it only if no other feature touched it; otherwise
  give it its own `scene(<name>):` commit after the feature commits.
- Never commit `.DS_Store`, `Library/`, `Temp/`, `Logs/`, or `UserSettings/`.

## Tags

When a feature reaches a state worth showing (first playable, visual pass,
final), suggest a lightweight tag named `<feature>-v<n>`, e.g. `scent-trails-v1`.
